Article 2 (Registration of Establishment of Sectional Superficies Based on Adjudication of Expropriation or Use)
(1) Where any of the following persons receives an adjudication of expropriation or use establishing sectional superficies pursuant to the Act on the Acquisition of Land, etc. for Public Works and the Compensation Therefor, that person may independently apply for registration of establishment of sectional superficies on the ground of expropriation of a right or use of land, by providing the written adjudication and information evidencing payment of compensation or deposit as attached information:
- An urban railroad constructor under subparagraph 7 of Article 2 of the Urban Railroad Act (hereinafter referred to as an "urban railroad constructor");
- A road management authority under subparagraph 5 of Article 2 of the Road Act (hereinafter referred to as a "road management authority");
- An electric utility business entity under subparagraph 2 of Article 2 of the Electric Utility Act (hereinafter referred to as an "electric utility business entity");
- An implementer of agricultural production infrastructure improvement projects under Article 10 of the Rearrangement of Agricultural and Fishing Villages Act (hereinafter referred to as an "agricultural infrastructure improvement project implementer");
- An implementer of railroad construction projects under Article 8 of the Act on the Construction of Railroads and Maintenance of Railroad Facilities (hereinafter referred to as a "railroad construction project implementer");
- An implementer of regional development projects under Article 19 of the Regional Development and Support Act (hereinafter referred to as a "regional development project implementer");
- A water supply business entity under subparagraph 21 of Article 3 of the Water Supply and Waterworks Installation Act (hereinafter referred to as a "water supply business entity");
- An electric power source development business entity under Article 3 of the Electric Power Source Development Promotion Act (hereinafter referred to as an "electric power source development business entity"); and
- A person intending to install public sewerage under Article 10-3 of the Sewerage Act (hereinafter referred to as a "person intending to install public sewerage"). <Amended on September 28, 2009; February 2, 2017; January 9, 2019; and October 29, 2021.>
(2) Even where the registration record of the land on which sectional superficies is to be established under paragraph (1) contains registration of a right to use or profit from the land or registration of a right whose subject matter is such a right, an application for registration of establishment of sectional superficies may be made without obtaining the consent of the holders of those rights. <Amended on September 28, 2009.>
